ask mechanics only; this is not diagnosis, treatment, injury prevention, isolated activation, or a guarantee of transfer."},"athleteSupport":{"whyItMatters":"Practises a compact controlled rock and return without making it a roll-to-stand.","primaryCue":"Hug your shins, make one slow back-and-forward rock, return to the same tuck, then reset.","secondaryCues":["keep the shape compact","do not push with your hands","do not load your head or neck","stop and reset between repetitions"],"expectedSensations":["trunk and front-of-hip effort","controlled back contact and orientation change","steady breathing after each return"],"unexpectedSensations":["sharp or increasing pain","dizziness, nausea, chest symptoms, unusual breathlessness, numbness, tingling, weakness, circulation change, or disorientation"],"selfChecks":["start and finish in the same supine tuck","one backward-forward return per repetition","no hand push-off","no head or neck loading","no stop symptom"],"accessibility":{"captionsRequired":true,"transcriptRequired":true,"stillSequenceRequired":true,"audioDescriptionRequired":true},"readingLevel":"plain_language"},"coachSupport":{"observationChecklist":["exact dynamic supine tuck rock rather than static hold, seated rock, roll, or stand-up","safe floor station and exit","contact path, hand use, head/neck loading, breathing, orientation, repetitions, symptoms, and first quality loss"],"faultCorrections":{"hand_push_off":"reset and reduce range or pace; do not count a push-assisted rock","head_neck_loading":"stop the rock and select another reviewed task if controlled back contact cannot be restored","loss_of_return":"reduce the range and count only an exact return to the same tuck"},"doNotUseWhen":["the requested task is static, seated, rolling to stand, loaded, assessment, or clinical","the exact dynamic task conflicts with current symptoms, restrictions, floor access, or communication"]},"supportOperations":{"issueCategories":["floor_access","contact_or_orien